title: "G4 Gaze: gaze sources, ft-gaze to ft-gazed to the pointer helper, the calibration panel, idle and wake (78e93b1)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Stopped, off, or nothing open
    lg1: Running or open, as it should be
    lg2: Between: waking, fitting, a lease running out
    lg3: Closed early: ignored, the headset off, quit
    lg4: Suspected open bug: the state that breaks the rule
    lg5: Z1 open, ScreensComeBack: ft-gazed dies during a full calibration (an exception in run, a SIGKILL). Nothing calls close(), and ft-screens' "hide" is a plain switch with no lease. The new ft-gazed never knew, so Frametop's screens stay hidden (red Z1.1-4, TLC Crash, 7 steps)
    lg6: Z2 open, FullOnlyWhenNeeded: our tracker's first calibration saves, and ft-gazed still holds ft-eyes' status from before the fit. If full_armed is still set, the next need_full opens a second full calibration at once. Calibrate never clears it, gaze mode coming on during the calibration sets it. 3a796b5 closed only the don's way in (red Z2.1-4, TLC Code 10 steps, CodeAuto 10, FitSays holds)
    lg7: Z3 open, minor: Check headset fit asked for while idle waits for a corrected gaze (svc.last_sample). Our tracker before its first calibration never sends one, so it opens only after the whole WAKE_SETTLE, 15 s (red Z3.1-2, from the code)
    lg8: Z4 open, CalibrationComes: no eyes for EYES_GONE (2 s) close the full calibration, but away needs AWAY_MIN (3 s). Eyes back in that second are no don, so nothing re-arms it and it never opens by itself again (red Z4.1-3, TLC Code 11 steps, Steam too, NoBlip holds)
    lg9: Holds at 78e93b1: IdleStops, CheckKeepsAwake in all 11 configs, ScreensComeBack without crashes, TrackerWakes without endless crashes. Fixed and drawn green: the 2026-10-05 deadlock (d39fbb9, PreBlind breaks CalibrationComes in 7 steps) and the don re-arming during a calibration (3a796b5, PreGuardAuto breaks FullOnlyWhenNeeded)
    lg10: Known limit, not a new bug: an eye-server.mmap layout ft-gaze doesn't know (NewLayout) blocks even our tracker's calibration, since its eyes seen come from mmap1. problem() says so in Input Settings
    lg11: Escape hatches: Z1, the screens hotkey (toggle), a VR game starting or ending, or the visibility setting reset g_manual. Z2, quit the second one (calquit, its calibration is saved). Z4, Calibrate or quickcal on the Gaze page
    lg12: Another group: arrows into it are where G4 touches it, drawn there, not here
  }
